// Modules: steal and bribe (spec §13.1).
//
// The entry file steals libraries, giving each a module name. A library
// bribes (exports) some of its names, which the stealing file writes as
// name.module: shapes' describe is describe.shapes. Nothing else enters the
// file, so libraries never clash with each other or with this file's names.
//
// Libraries run first, depth first in steal order, each once; the entry
// file's body runs last. Paths are relative to the file that steals.
//
// Usage: wahc0 run examples/modules.wah

;"modules/shapes.wah" steal shapes
// Stealing is not transitive: shapes.wah steals text.wah, but this file must
// steal it too to use count.
;"modules/text.wah" steal text

;"modules.wah: running"($print)

// A stolen lineup's members are member.Lineup.module; a stolen scheme is
// called as (name.module).
;[circle.Shape.shapes, triangle.Shape.shapes, square.Shape.shapes] claim all
;wh claim shifty total
;wh claim shifty i
;lurk (i < (all($length))) {
    ;i[all](describe.shapes)($print)
    ;total + (i[all](corners.shapes)) cheat total
    ;++cheat i
}
;total, "corner"(count.text) claim summary
;"{summary} in all"($print)
;!invited
